# SEO Safe Mode

Before any SEO-related change, read `docs/seo/SEO-SAFE-MODE.md`.

## Required

- Keep Safe Mode invariant flags false unless the user explicitly authorizes leaving Safe Mode.
- Prefer technical crawl/head infrastructure over content or layout changes.
- SEO-7 must not deploy SEO-8 marketing title/description rewrites. Proposed copy stays in `docs/seo/proposed-metadata.md` with `PENDING_APPROVAL`.
- Canonical origin is always `https://www.mccoy.nl`. Never emit preview/localhost/admin hosts as canonical.
- IndexNow: production `www.mccoy.nl` URLs only; publish remains successful if notify fails.

## Forbidden without explicit authorization

Do not edit for SEO:

- `packages/cms-renderer` (including block views, `RegisteredBlockView`, `SitePageSections`)
- Block registries / fixed↔block compatibility
- CMS migration / MG5 apply logic
- Translation schema or overlay mutations for SEO copy
- Producten content, Aanvragen, authentication

`scripts/seo/safe-mode-diff-guard.mjs` must pass for SEO qualification.

## Out of scope shortcuts

- No MG5 apply, no MR kickoff from SEO work
- No invented JSON-LD reviews, ratings, or prices
- No visible body/copy/styling changes “for SEO”
